      "excerpt": "During the three months ended September 26, 2026, two end customers individually accounted for 37% and 11% of our total net revenue, respectively. During the three months ended September 27, 2025, two end customers individually accounted for 22% and 21% of our total net revenue, respectively. We had no other end customers that represented 10% or greater of our total net revenue for the respective periods. Revenue by Region We operate in three geographic regions: Americas, Asia-Pacific, and EMEA (Europe, Middle East, and Africa). Net revenue is assigned to the geographic region and country where our product is initially shipped. For example, certain customers may request shipment of our product to a contract manufacturer in one country, which may differ from the location of their end customers. The following table presents net revenue by the three geographic regions we operate in and net revenue from countries that generally represented 10% or more of our total net revenue based on customer shipping locations (in millions, except percentage data): Three Months Ended September 26, 2026 September 27, 2025 Amount % of Total Amount % of Total Net revenue: Americas: United States $ 297.4 23.6 % $ 93.7 17.6 % Mexico 230.8 18.3 73.6 13.8 Other Americas 1.1 0.1 8.6 1.6 Total Americas $ 529.3 42.0 % $ 175.9 33.0 % Asia-Pacific: Hong Kong $ 187.1 14.8 % $ 92.9 17.4 % Thailand 227.5 18.0 109.1 20.4 China 162.0 12.8 49.3 9.2 Japan 39.0 3.1 21.0 3.9 Other Asia-Pacific 69.9 5.5 49.4 9.3 Total Asia-Pacific $ 685.5 54.2 % $ 321.7 60.2 % EMEA $ 47.8 3.8 % $ 36.2 6.8 % Total net revenue $ 1,262.6 100.0 % $ 533.8 100.0 % 51 For the three months ended September 26, 2026, net revenue from customers outside the United States, based on customer shipping locations, represented 76.4% of net revenue. Our net revenue is primarily denominated in U.S. dollars, including our net revenue from customers outside the United States as presented above. We expect revenue from customers outside of the United States to continue to be an important part of our overall net revenue and an increasing focus for net revenue growth opportunities. However, regulatory and enforcement actions by the United States and other governmental agencies, as well as changes in tax and trade policies and tariffs, have impacted and may continue to negatively impact net revenue from customers outside the United States.",
